    {
      "name": "highlight-prefetch/selected_startup_ms",
      "reason": "Accepted for 0.20.0 because the five-sample snapshots landed in different scheduler-dependent startup clusters: 0.19.1 had four 10–12ms samples and one 22.58ms sample (median 11.08ms), while 0.20.0 had two 10ms samples and three 22–23ms samples (median 22.06ms). Both snapshots used Bun 1.3.14 on Linux x64. A controlled, order-balanced 20-pair A/B on the same machine between v0.19.1 (a20ae938) and 0.20.0 HEAD (15ff4622) measured selected-startup medians of 24.02ms and 24.19ms respectively (HEAD +0.17ms/+0.7%; paired median delta +0.03ms; 11/20 HEAD samples slower), while next-file readiness improved from 69.62ms to 68.91ms. Because the benchmark timer spans asynchronous render and zero-delay sleep scheduling, the five-sample median crossed timing clusters rather than revealing a selected-highlight slowdown."
    }
